## Why This Is Asked
This checks real-world ability to design multi-cloud patterns with clean module boundaries and governance.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform modules, provider aliases, multi-cloud strategy
- Environment backends and per-environment isolation
- CI gates, version constraints, governance for cloud support

## Code Example
```terraform
provider "aws" {
  alias   = "aws"
  version = "~> 4.0"
  region  = var.aws_region
}
provider "google" {
  alias   = "google"
  version = "~> 4.0"
  project = var.gcp_project
}
provider "azurerm" {
  alias    = "azure"
  version  = "~> 3.0"
  features {}
}
module "monitors" {
  source       = "./modules/monitors"
  cloud_config = {
    aws   = { region = var.aws_region, enabled = true }
    gcp   = { region = var.gcp_region, enabled = true }
    azure = { region = var.azure_region, enabled = true }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cross-cloud drift in this pattern?
- How would you extend to add a new cloud while keeping tight approvals?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design modular, environment-scoped infrastructure with a simple map-driven pattern, a common practice at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform modules and for_each with maps
- Conditional resource configuration via variables
- Environment-specific variable files and CI gates
- Minimal code references for quick in-repo patterns

## Code Example
```terraform
# wrapper module
variable "env_buckets" { type = map(object{ name_prefix string; versioning bool; encryption bool }) }
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "env" {
  for_each = var.env_buckets
  bucket   = "${each.key}-${each.value.name_prefix}"
  acl      = "private"
  versioning {
    enabled = each.value.versioning
  }
  dynamic "server_side_encryption_configuration" {
    for_each = each.value.encryption ? [1] : []
    content {
      rule { apply_server_side_encryption_by_default { sse_algorithm = "AES256" } }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate env_buckets inputs in CI before plan?
- How would you handle bucket naming collisions across environments?
